(1) (Enforcement date) This Act shall enter into force six months after the date of its promulgation.
(2) (Transitional measures concerning reporting) Any report or personal card which is already made or submitted to the head of a local government with respect to a missing child, etc. or a child, etc. whose custodian is not ascertained, before this Act enters into force, shall be deemed made or submitted pursuant to Article 6 (1) and (3).
(3) (Transitional measures concerning genetic testing) The taking of a test sample, genetic testing and the management of genetic information conducted with respect to a missing child, etc. before this Act enters into force shall be deemed conducted pursuant to Article 11.

